    "explanation": "Rider: your $4.00 no-show cancellation fee is refunded in full. Driver: the fee does not stand, and no compensation is payable.\n\nWHY THE FEE FALLS. POL-NS-01 is conjunctive — every limb must hold, and limb (b) does not. Limb (b) asks the GPS trace to place the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius at or before the 08:12:35 'arrived' event, using at least three consecutive fixes accurate to 25 m or better. EV-GPS-00212 is complete and unimpaired (weight 1.0: 93 fixes, 100% coverage, 0 s maximum gap, 10 s cadence, rider track present), but every fix in it fails the 25 m accuracy filter — the Raffles Place urban canyon — so qualifying_fix_count is 0 and the longest qualifying run is 0.0 s. On POL-NS-02's own terms there is no qualifying in-radius fix, the driver is not deemed to have arrived, limb (b) fails, and the rider is entitled to a full refund. The amount is the fare_breakdown cancellation_fee of 4.00 (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00). The driver's 'arrived' marker satisfies limb (a) and the cancellation code EXCESSIVE_WAIT satisfies limb (d), but limb (a) is only the marker; the arrival test and the clock run from the GPS, and here no admissible fix falls in the geofence. POL-NS-06 gives the same outcome independently: the effective in-geofence dwell is 0 s against the 300 s STANDARD minimum, a 300 s shortfall, and that clause refunds in full whether or not the rider was present or responsive.\n\nON THE DISPUTED POINTS. (1) Poor accuracy is not an integrity defect: the trace is not impaired under POL-NS-08(a)–(d) — no clock skew beyond 90 s, no gap over 120 s, 93 fixes, rider track present — so no POL-NS-09(e) escalation arises and no weight below 1.0 caps confidence (POL-GEN-02(2)); this is a failure of the clause's arrival test, not an admissibility failure. (2) The driver's POL-NS-09(b) escalation argument is declined: POL-NS-02 resolves the tension between the trip record's 'arrived' marker and the trace, because that marker is limb (a) only and arrival is governed by the GPS limb — the conflict is not one 'no clause resolves'. (3) POL-NS-03 does not rescue the charge: even on its facts it refunds the fee in full, and because the rider named 'exit A', matching the pickup label 'Raffles Place MRT (Exit A)', limb (i) would deny the driver compensation in any event; the 2.00 pin-ambiguity goodwill (POL-NS-03(ii)) does not arise, as registered_pickup_points is 1 and the rider did name the entrance. (4) POL-NS-07 compensation is refused: it requires POL-NS-01 satisfied in full, which it is not, and the anti-farming check does not trip anyway (no_show_terminations_30d 2 of completed_trips_30d 132 = 1.5%, below both 4 and 0.08); only those two named counters were used, and the driver's prior_no_show_flags, rating and acceptance_rate were rightly treated as context only (POL-GEN-01). (5) POL-NS-04 is not in play: the driver replied 28 seconds after the rider's locating message, inside the 120 s window, defeating limb (b) — both sides agree. (6) POL-NS-05 is not engaged (no false marker established), so no false-arrival record is referred. (7) The $4.00 is correctly computed under fee_schedule.resolution_rule — the greater of the STANDARD zone fee (4.00) and the RYDE_X tier fee (4.00), a tie — so no POL-NS-08(d) defect exists; but a correctly computed fee is not chargeable where limb (b) fails. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00212-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0); it is cited only for its absence and carries no fact, and it does not block the base shortfall under POL-NS-06.\n\nNo referral is made, because no clause produces one on these facts: POL-NS-05(ii) is not engaged and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming escalation is not tripped. The charge is reversed in full: SGD 4.00 to the rider."
